  "text": "This is not advice, I'm just trying to be helpful. I've seen this comment a lot in the last 24 hours. We are acutely aware of the issues around sports betting and taxes as we actually profit and we have to pay taxes and we'd like to do so in a professional manner. So we pay to get information. In a recent thing I went to to learn about this very thing, this came up. Amateur gamblers state In this list of states, this was given directly from a tax attorney. In this list of states, you cannot write off your losses if you're an amateur gambler, which 99% of you are going to fall into. Make sure you're doing your research, make sure you understand. This can obviously lead to some pretty big issues, so make sure if you're living in one of these states you understand the tax implications of sports betting. Again, not advice, just trying to help those that want it.",
